diff --git a/research.md b/research.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d71de47
--- /dev/null
+++ b/research.md
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+# Live compatibility research record
+
+Accessed 2026-08-14. The sources cover compatibility, interoperability, sizing, upgrade guidance, and Edge availability.
+
+- **Broadcom VMware Compatibility Guide** — https://compatibilityguide.broadcom.com/ — Accessed 2026-08-14. Consulted the live entry point for the current VCF/vSphere hardware compatibility and Product Interoperability Matrix guidance; used to confirm that compatibility claims need a current matrix check in addition to the pinned design authority.
+- **Unified VCF Product Releases & Versioning (Broadcom KB 410435)** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/410435/unified-vcf-product-releases-versioning.html — Accessed 2026-08-14. Confirmed that VCF 9.0 BOM components use the unified 9.0 release convention and cadence, informing the component-version set and lifecycle review.
+- **Correlating VMware Cloud Foundation version with constituent product versions (Broadcom KB 314608)** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/314608/correlating-vmware-cloud-foundation-vers.html — Accessed 2026-08-14. Checked the live VCF release/BOM mapping and available 9.0 maintenance releases when reviewing supported forward paths.
+- **Lifecycle Management for VMware Cloud Foundation 9.0** — https://techdocs.broadcom.com/us/en/vmware-cis/vcf/vcf-9-0-and-later/9-0/lifecycle-management.html — Accessed 2026-08-14. Confirmed the published starting-version and staged-upgrade guidance; because this inventory is greenfield, used it as a forward lifecycle check rather than adding a migration plan.
+- **VMware Cloud Foundation NSX-T Edge Node Virtual Machine Resizing Tool (Broadcom KB 312196)** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/312196/vmware-cloud-foundation-nsxt-edge-node-v.html — Accessed 2026-08-14. Confirmed VCF Edge clusters use a consistent VM form factor and that sizing or expansion changes are managed as Edge-cluster lifecycle operations.
+- **NSX Edge dvportgroup disappeared during a VCF 9.0 restart (Broadcom KB 409148)** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/409148 — Accessed 2026-08-14. Confirmed the two Edge datapath port-group pattern with opposing active/standby uplinks; this supports the independent-fabric mapping in the design.
